allenging to commit this\n  strategy to a specific release until that dependency is delivered.\" The go/no-go gate (E001) is\n  correctly P0 and first — do not let the release-pending status force starting a provisioning\n  branch before the gate resolves.\n- **Scope trap avoided**: the AI-generated strategy's image build + Konflux onboarding chain\n  (1–2 sprints) was eliminated by Staff Engineer Correction 2 — the pgvector-capable image already\n  exists. Any re-introduction of image-building scope should be challenged.\n- **Multi-tenant scoping**: the strategy's open question on per-namespace vs per-instance scoping\n  is largely resolved by Staff direction (per-namespace preferred; the per-instance driver —\n  Auto Rag — is decoupled), but it is confirmed as part of the E001 decision record rather than\n  assumed.\n- **Open question retained as documentation scope**: the migration-path question (alignment with\n  commonly-used vector DB providers) is resolved as a configurable-connection AC plus\n  documentation (E005), not as a gating investigation — the pgvector default already aligns with\n  commonly-used providers and migration is configuration, not new code.\n\n## Tiered Delivery\n\nExternal dependency with uncertain timing: RHAISTRAT-7164 (dashboard operator modularization).\nPartial value is deliverable without it, so the strategy splits:\n\n- **Tier 1 (independent, start immediately)**: E001 (go/no-go decision — sprint-planning gate),\n  E002 (OGX distribution pgvector provider), E003 (playground wiring, works against any\n  PostgreSQL endpoint including bring-your-own), E004 (benchmark and sizing — risk-reduction\n  validation).\n- **Tier 2 (dependency-gated)**: the provisioning branch epics (BRANCH-A-E006 / BRANCH-B-E006),\n  gated by the E001 decision; BRANCH-A-E006 is additionally preconditioned on RHAISTRAT-7164\n  actually delivering the operator layer.\n- **E005 (documentation)** runs last, blocked by the Tier 1 Implementations and the E001 decisi