n, and portability to the platform-provided shared\n  PostgreSQL planned for RHOAI 3.6).\n- Confirm the scoping model for the default vector store (per-namespace vs per-OGXServer-instance).\n  Per-namespace is the working direction per the component lead's preference for isolation; the\n  main per-instance driver (Auto Rag) has been decoupled from this strategy.\n- Record the outcome as a decision record (selected provisioning mechanism, scoping model, and\n  rationale) that selects the downstream provisioning implementation.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Go/no-go criteria and a decision date for the RHAISTRAT-7164 dependency are documented and\n  agreed in sprint planning before the decision is made.\n- A decision record exists that selects exactly one provisioning approach (operator-based,\n  BFF-managed, or bring-your-own) with rationale grounded in RHAISTRAT-7164's actual delivery\n  status.\n- The scoping model (per-namespace or per-instance) is confirmed in the same decision record.\n- The decision is socialized with the Gen AI Studio lead and the engineering team, and the\n  selected downstream provisioning work is unblocked (or explicitly descoped to a\n  bring-your-own posture with documentation).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- AC-5 (multi-tenant scoping, e.g. per-namespace isolation) — scoping model confirmation.\n- SE-1 / SE-2 (provisioning pattern selection and bring-your-own fallback) — go/no-go decision.\n- SE-6 (no additional manual setup steps) — the decision determines whether manual setup can be\n  avoided entirely.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":74347,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b30c0eb90956327c","agent_id":"abdf0a0fcd4c2ca8d","session_id":"546378e3-e46e-4fda-8937-a306cf6cc87c","uuid":"ace6c8d2-15ec-4a77-83b9-bfdcebfda159","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:04:36.352Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHA