{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-590d2279-5d4d-47b3-adb7-b182a9424a19","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a5611e8b8e4da12f","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8004-kkcvpu4k/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8004-E002.md","content":"# Enable and Validate the Remote pgvector vector_io Provider in the OGX Distribution\n\n## Description\n\nMake the remote pgvector vector store provider available and activatable in the RHOAI OGX\ndistribution so that Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows can use a PostgreSQL/pgvector endpoint\nas their vector store, replacing the inline Milvus provider that is being removed from the\ndistribution (RHAISTRAT-7474). Per the Staff Engineer Input, the existing remote vector store\nimplementation can be largely reused for pgvector integration — the provider work is focused\nenablement and validation, not a new integration program. The vector store must run as a separate\nprocess from the OGX instance (remote provider, not inline).\n\n## Scope\n\n- Verify the remote pgvector vector_io provider (`remote::pgvector`, activated via the\n  `ENABLE_PGVECTOR` environment guard) is present and shippable in the RHOAI OGX distribution\n  build configuration (the distribution already ships only remote-capable vector providers —\n  Milvus, PGVector, Qdrant — and strips inline ones).\n- Fix any gaps in the activation path, provider configuration schema, or connection handling\n  (connection string / secret, TLS) needed for the provider to work against a PostgreSQL instance\n  with the pgvector extension.\n- Verify any required database-side initialization performed by the provider (e.g. vector table\n  schema creation) works against the Red Hat `rhel9/postgresql-16` image, which includes pgvector\n  out of the box — no custom image build is in scope.\n- Validate the provider end-to-end with representative playground RAG operations (document\n  ingestion and retrieval over small document sets, consistent with dev-experimentation usage).\n- Explicitly out of scope: application storage changes (OGX application storage remains SQLite —\n  vector storage and application storage are independent configurations), any inline provider\n  work, and any image build or pipeline onboarding.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- An OGX distribution build can be launched with the remote pgvector vector_io provider activated\n  and configured with a PostgreSQL connection, with no inline vector provider involved.\n- Vector insert and similarity-search operations through the distribution's vector I/O API succeed\n  against a PostgreSQL instance running the pgvector extension.\n- The pgvector-backed vector store runs as a separate process, decoupled from the OGX server\n  process.\n- The provider works with flat scan (no index) for typical playground document-set sizes, per the\n  dev-experimentation performance scope.\n- Any distribution configuration changes are covered by tests and documented in the distribution's\n  configuration reference.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- AC-2 (playground RAG workflows function with the default vector store, no loss of capability) —\n  provider capability foundation.\n- AC-4 (vector store runs as a separate process, decoupled from the OGX instance) — remote\n  provider architecture.\n- SE-5 (vector_io configuration only; application storage unchanged).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":75254,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b30c0eb90956327c","agent_id":"abdf0a0fcd4c2ca8d","session_id":"546378e3-e46e-4fda-8937-a306cf6cc87c","uuid":"8800a8e5-3361-4aa2-9eb8-821be6c2bcfd","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:04:51.548Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8004"}
