ed explicit-connection configuration.\n- Design for portability: when a platform-provided shared PostgreSQL becomes available (planned\n  RHOAI 3.6), the same wiring consumes the shared connection string rather than a\n  self-provisioned instance — no rework of the provider configuration path.\n- Keep OGX application storage configuration unchanged (SQLite defaults); no storage migration.\n- Integration validation: playground RAG workflows (document upload, ingestion, retrieval) run\n  end-to-end against a pgvector-backed vector store with no loss of current capability compared\n  to the inline-provider experience.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A Gen AI Studio playground with RAG enabled runs its OGXServer instance with the vector_io\n  provider configured for remote pgvector, using the PostgreSQL connection secret in the\n  playground namespace.\n- Playground RAG workflows (document ingestion and retrieval) function end-to-end against the\n  pgvector vector store with no loss of current capability.\n- The vector store used by the playground runs as a separate process from the OGX instance.\n- When a user supplies PostgreSQL connection details in the OGXServer CR spec, the playground\n  uses that database for its vector store (bring-your-own support).\n- OGX application storage settings for playground OGXServer instances are unchanged from their\n  current defaults (no SQLite-to-PostgreSQL migration).\n- The connection-secret contract is documented so any provisioning mechanism can satisfy it.\n- End-to-end validation is performed against an OGX distribution build that includes the remote\n  pgvector vector_io provider.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- AC-2 (playground RAG workflows function with the default vector store, no loss of capability).\n- AC-4 (vector store runs as a separate process, decoupled from the OGX instance).\n- SE-2 (bring-your-own PostgreSQL via user-configured connection secret).\n- SE-3 (migration path: connection is configurable, enabling later move to an external\n  production-grade vector database).\n- SE-4 (portability to the platform-provided shared connection string in RHOAI 3.6).\n- SE-5 (vector_io configuration only; application storage remains SQLite).\n- SE-6 (no additional manual setup steps for the provisioned path).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":76068,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b30c0eb90956327c","agent_id":"abdf0a0fcd4c2ca8d","session_id":"546378e3-e46e-4fda-8937-a306cf6cc87c","uuid":"5bfbc6b9-6301-44d4-8020-6253a33c1394","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:05:09.676Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8004"}
