{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-c2df169c-f593-4719-8526-839cf0ac6266","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a735129720be207","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8004-kkcvpu4k/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8004-E004.md","content":"# Benchmark pgvector Against the Inline Milvus Baseline for Playground RAG and Recommend Resource Sizing\n\n## Description\n\nValidate that pgvector is an acceptable default vector store for Gen AI Studio playground RAG\nworkloads in dev-experimentation scope, and produce the resource-sizing recommendation for the\ndefault PostgreSQL/pgvector instance. Per the Staff Engineer Input, strict latency SLAs are not\nrequired: the benchmark captures the inline Milvus baseline (before it is removed from the\ndistribution) and verifies pgvector performs in the same order of magnitude on representative\nplayground workloads. Typical playground usage involves small document sets, for which flat scan\n(no index) is expected to be sufficient. This is a Tier 1 risk-reduction validation that runs in\nparallel with the implementation work; its sizing output feeds the provisioning implementations\nas tuning input (they start from the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL resource\nrequests/limits as the reference).\n\n## Scope\n\n- Build a repeatable benchmark harness for representative playground RAG operations (document\n  ingestion and similarity search over small document sets) exercised through the OGX vector I/O\n  API.\n- Capture the inline Milvus provider baseline on the same workload before inline providers are\n  removed from the distribution.\n- Run the same workload against a PostgreSQL/pgvector backend (flat scan, no index) and compare\n  order of magnitude.\n- Record PostgreSQL resource consumption (CPU/memory) under the benchmark workload and recommend\n  resource requests/limits, using the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL resource\n  requests/limits as the starting reference.\n- Document results and a go/no-go-style assessment: is pgvector acceptable as the\n  dev-experimentation default, or does the gap warrant revisiting the default-store choice.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The inline Milvus baseline is captured on the representative workload and recorded before\n  inline provider removal.\n- pgvector results on the same workload are recorded and compared; pgvector is within the same\n  order of magnitude as the baseline for playground-scale document sets (no specific latency\n  threshold applies — dev-experimentation scope).\n- A resource-sizing recommendation for the default PostgreSQL/pgvector instance is produced,\n  starting from the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL requests/limits and adjusted based on\n  the measured consumption.\n- Benchmark harness and results are documented well enough to be re-run when sizing needs\n  revisiting.\n- Users with production-scale vector workloads are noted as out of scope for the default store\n  (they should use an external vector database) — recorded in the findings.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- AC-2 (no loss of current capability) — measurement basis for the no-regression claim.\n- AC-6 (lightweight enough for resource-constrained environments) — sizing recommendation.\n- SE-7 (order-of-magnitude benchmark, flat scan acceptable, no strict SLAs).\n- SE-8 (resource sizing from model-registry-operator reference, adjusted per benchmark).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":77054,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b30c0eb90956327c","agent_id":"abdf0a0fcd4c2ca8d","session_id":"546378e3-e46e-4fda-8937-a306cf6cc87c","uuid":"349bdbca-0076-4ff9-8120-da086ac89303","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:05:24.414Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8004"}
