on secret in the playground namespace, satisfying the\n  connection-secret contract consumed by the playground OGXServer vector_io wiring.\n- Set resource requests/limits starting from the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL reference\n  values, adjusted per benchmark findings.\n- Handle lifecycle: provisioning on demand, and cleanup/garbage collection when the playground\n  (or its namespace) is removed.\n- Document the provisioning behavior for inclusion in the user-facing documentation.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A Gen AI Studio playground with RAG enabled gets a working PostgreSQL/pgvector instance\n  provisioned automatically, with no manual user setup, in a cluster with the operator installed.\n- The provisioned instance uses the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL image with pgvector (no custom\n  image build, no new pipeline onboarding).\n- The connection secret satisfies the contract consumed by the playground OGXServer vector_io\n  wiring, and playground RAG works end-to-end against the provisioned instance.\n- Instances are scoped per the confirmed scoping model (per-namespace isolation by default) —\n  tenants in different namespaces do not share vector data.\n- Resource requests/limits start from the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL reference values\n  and are recorded with rationale (benchmark-adjusted where available).\n- Provisioned resources are cleaned up when the playground is deleted.\n- Disconnected-install support: the PostgreSQL image reference is resolvable via the\n  related-image environment variable pattern.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- AC-1 (default vector store available out-of-the-box, no manual provisioning).\n- AC-2 (playground RAG workflows function with the default vector store) — provisioning completes\n  the end-to-end path.\n- AC-5 (multi-tenant scoping, per-namespace isolation).\n- AC-6 (lightweight for resource-constrained environments) — resource sizing.\n- SE-1 (model-registry-operator auto-provisioning pattern, no custom image).\n- SE-6 (no additional manual setup steps).\n- SE-8 (resource sizing from model-registry-operator reference).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":78575,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b30c0eb90956327c","agent_id":"abdf0a0fcd4c2ca8d","session_id":"546378e3-e46e-4fda-8937-a306cf6cc87c","uuid":"5977e6d9-cc20-46f4-9b79-a20938459abc","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:05:56.107Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8004"}
