{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a0d7c3be7aad7a68","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n3\ttitle: Default vector store provisioning approach go/no-go decision\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n5\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n6\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 0\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -2\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Default Vector Store Provisioning Approach Go/No-Go Decision\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation resolves the single largest uncertainty in the default vector store strategy:\n30\thow the PostgreSQL/pgvector instance for Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows gets provisioned\n31\tfor the target release. The Staff Engineer Input established that operator-based self-provisioning\n32\t(following the model-registry-operator pattern) requires a RHOAI-controlled operator layer that\n33\tonly the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164, In Progress) can provide, and that this\n34\tis a hard dependency with uncertain timing. If that dependency does not land in time, the fallback\n35\toptions are BFF-managed provisioning (the gen-ai BFF creates the PostgreSQL resources directly,\n36\tas it already does for guardrails infrastructure) or requiring customers to bring their own\n37\tPostgreSQL. The Staff Engineer Input directs the development team to define a go/no-go gate for\n38\tthis decision as part of sprint planning.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Define explicit go/no-go criteria and a decision date for whether the dashboard operator\n43\t  modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) will deliver the RHOAI-controlled operator layer in time for the\n44\t  target release (RHOAI 3.5).\n45\t- Track RHAISTRAT-7164 delivery status and confidence against those criteria.\n46\t- If the outcome is \"no-go\": decide between BFF-managed PostgreSQL provisioning and a\n47\t  bring-your-own-PostgreSQL posture, evaluating the BFF-managed approach's known caveats\n48\t  (lifecycle management without a reconciliation loop: cleanup on playground deletion, pod\n49\t  restart handling, credential rotation, and portability to the platform-provided shared\n50\t  PostgreSQL planned for RHOAI 3.6).\n51\t- Confirm the scoping model for the default vector store (per-namespace vs per-OGXServer-instance).\n52\t  Per-namespace is the working direction per the component lead's preference for isolation; the\n53\t  main per-instance driver (Auto Rag) has been decoupled from this strategy.\n54\t- Record the outcome as a decision record (selected provisioning mechanism, scoping model, and\n55\t  rationale) that selects the downstream provisioning implementation.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- Go/no-go criteria and a decision date for the RHAISTRAT-7164 dependency are documented and\n60\t  agreed in sprint planning before the decision is made.\n61\t- A decision record exists that selects exactly one provisioning approach (operator-based,\n62\t  BFF-managed, or bring-your-own) with rationale grounded in RHAISTRAT-7164's actual delivery\n63\t  status.\n64\t- The scoping model (per-namespace or per-instance) is confirmed in the same decision record.\n65\t- The decision is socialized with the Gen AI Studio lead and the engineering team, and the\n66\t  selected downstream provisioning work is unblocked (or explicitly descoped to a\n67\t  bring-your-own posture with documentation).\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability\n70\t\n71\t- AC-5 (multi-tenant scoping, e.g. per-namespace isolation) — scoping model confirmation.\n72\t- SE-1 / SE-2 (provisioning pattern selection and bring-your-own fallback) — go/no-go decision.\n73\t- SE-6 (no additional manual setup steps) — the decision determines whether manual setup can be\n74\t  avoided entirely.\n75\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a5d9e3a32beb111a","agent_id":"a9d1510e518acea17","session_id":"546378e3-e46e-4fda-8937-a306cf6cc87c","uuid":"2d4ce0cd-1b13-4f3b-b95e-70706179c7af","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:09:38.648Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a0d7c3be7aad7a68","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
