{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba60025010592778","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-E002\n3\ttitle: Enable and validate the remote pgvector vector_io provider in the OGX distribution\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n5\tcomponent: OGX Core\n6\tteam: OGX Core\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 0\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 7\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Enable and Validate the Remote pgvector vector_io Provider in the OGX Distribution\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tMake the remote pgvector vector store provider available and activatable in the RHOAI OGX\n34\tdistribution so that Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows can use a PostgreSQL/pgvector endpoint\n35\tas their vector store, replacing the inline Milvus provider that is being removed from the\n36\tdistribution (RHAISTRAT-7474). Per the Staff Engineer Input, the existing remote vector store\n37\timplementation can be largely reused for pgvector integration — the provider work is focused\n38\tenablement and validation, not a new integration program. The vector store must run as a separate\n39\tprocess from the OGX instance (remote provider, not inline).\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Verify the remote pgvector vector_io provider (`remote::pgvector`, activated via the\n44\t  `ENABLE_PGVECTOR` environment guard) is present and shippable in the RHOAI OGX distribution\n45\t  build configuration (the distribution already ships only remote-capable vector providers —\n46\t  Milvus, PGVector, Qdrant — and strips inline ones).\n47\t- Fix any gaps in the activation path, provider configuration schema, or connection handling\n48\t  (connection string / secret, TLS) needed for the provider to work against a PostgreSQL instance\n49\t  with the pgvector extension.\n50\t- Verify any required database-side initialization performed by the provider (e.g. vector table\n51\t  schema creation) works against the Red Hat `rhel9/postgresql-16` image, which includes pgvector\n52\t  out of the box — no custom image build is in scope.\n53\t- Validate the provider end-to-end with representative playground RAG operations (document\n54\t  ingestion and retrieval over small document sets, consistent with dev-experimentation usage).\n55\t- Explicitly out of scope: application storage changes (OGX application storage remains SQLite —\n56\t  vector storage and application storage are independent configurations), any inline provider\n57\t  work, and any image build or pipeline onboarding.\n58\t\n59\t## Acceptance Criteria\n60\t\n61\t- An OGX distribution build can be launched with the remote pgvector vector_io provider activated\n62\t  and configured with a PostgreSQL connection, with no inline vector provider involved.\n63\t- Vector insert and similarity-search operations through the distribution's vector I/O API succeed\n64\t  against a PostgreSQL instance running the pgvector extension.\n65\t- The pgvector-backed vector store runs as a separate process, decoupled from the OGX server\n66\t  process.\n67\t- The provider works with flat scan (no index) for typical playground document-set sizes, per the\n68\t  dev-experimentation performance scope.\n69\t- Any distribution configuration changes are covered by tests and documented in the distribution's\n70\t  configuration reference.\n71\t\n72\t## HLR Traceability\n73\t\n74\t- AC-2 (playground RAG workflows function with the default vector store, no loss of capability) —\n75\t  provider capability foundation.\n76\t- AC-4 (vector store runs as a separate process, decoupled from the OGX instance) — remote\n77\t  provider architecture.\n78\t- SE-5 (vector_io configuration only; application storage unchanged).\n79\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a5d9e3a32beb111a","agent_id":"a9d1510e518acea17","session_id":"546378e3-e46e-4fda-8937-a306cf6cc87c","uuid":"d66dca5d-cbe1-4868-af15-f0f1b1d18e94","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:09:39.495Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba60025010592778","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
