{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-adceadaf824ea214","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-E003\n3\ttitle: Configure Gen AI Studio playground OGXServer instances to use a pgvector vector\n4\t  store\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n6\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n7\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tdependencies: []\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 7\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Configure Gen AI Studio Playground OGXServer Instances to Use a pgvector Vector Store\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tWire the pgvector vector store into Gen AI Studio playgrounds: when the gen-ai BFF creates and\n35\tconfigures OGXServer instances for the playground, it configures the vector_io provider for\n36\tremote pgvector using the PostgreSQL connection secret available in the playground namespace.\n37\tThe wiring is mechanism-agnostic — it consumes a connection secret regardless of whether that\n38\tPostgreSQL was provisioned by a platform operator, by the BFF itself, or supplied by the user —\n39\tso it delivers independent value (including a bring-your-own-PostgreSQL posture) and does not\n40\twait on the provisioning-approach decision. Per the Staff Engineer Input, the vector_io provider\n41\tconfiguration is completely independent of OGX application storage: the BFF's existing SQLite\n42\tapplication-storage defaults for OGXServer instances remain untouched.\n43\t\n44\t## Scope\n45\t\n46\t- Extend the gen-ai BFF's OGXServer instance creation/configuration (currently in the code path\n47\t  that sets storage defaults) to configure the vector_io provider as remote pgvector, activated\n48\t  and connected via the PostgreSQL connection secret present in the playground namespace.\n49\t- Define and document the connection-secret contract (name/format) that any provisioning\n50\t  mechanism — platform operator, BFF self-provisioning, or user-supplied bring-your-own\n51\t  configuration via the OGXServer CR spec — must satisfy.\n52\t- Respect user-supplied PostgreSQL connection details in the OGXServer CR spec when present\n53\t  (bring-your-own support), aligned with OGX 1.0's supported explicit-connection configuration.\n54\t- Design for portability: when a platform-provided shared PostgreSQL becomes available (planned\n55\t  RHOAI 3.6), the same wiring consumes the shared connection string rather than a\n56\t  self-provisioned instance — no rework of the provider configuration path.\n57\t- Keep OGX application storage configuration unchanged (SQLite defaults); no storage migration.\n58\t- Integration validation: playground RAG workflows (document upload, ingestion, retrieval) run\n59\t  end-to-end against a pgvector-backed vector store with no loss of current capability compared\n60\t  to the inline-provider experience.\n61\t\n62\t## Acceptance Criteria\n63\t\n64\t- A Gen AI Studio playground with RAG enabled runs its OGXServer instance with the vector_io\n65\t  provider configured for remote pgvector, using the PostgreSQL connection secret in the\n66\t  playground namespace.\n67\t- Playground RAG workflows (document ingestion and retrieval) function end-to-end against the\n68\t  pgvector vector store with no loss of current capability.\n69\t- The vector store used by the playground runs as a separate process from the OGX instance.\n70\t- When a user supplies PostgreSQL connection details in the OGXServer CR spec, the playground\n71\t  uses that database for its vector store (bring-your-own support).\n72\t- OGX application storage settings for playground OGXServer instances are unchanged from their\n73\t  current defaults (no SQLite-to-PostgreSQL migration).\n74\t- The connection-secret contract is documented so any provisioning mechanism can satisfy it.\n75\t- End-to-end validation is performed against an OGX distribution build that includes the remote\n76\t  pgvector vector_io provider.\n77\t\n78\t## HLR Traceability\n79\t\n80\t- AC-2 (playground RAG workflows function with the default vector store, no loss of capability).\n81\t- AC-4 (vector store runs as a separate process, decoupled from the OGX instance).\n82\t- SE-2 (bring-your-own PostgreSQL via user-configured connection secret).\n83\t- SE-3 (migration path: connection is configurable, enabling later move to an external\n84\t  production-grade vector database).\n85\t- SE-4 (portability to the platform-provided shared connection string in RHOAI 3.6).\n86\t- SE-5 (vector_io configuration only; application storage remains SQLite).\n87\t- SE-6 (no additional manual setup steps for the provisioned path).\n88\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a5d9e3a32beb111a","agent_id":"a9d1510e518acea17","session_id":"546378e3-e46e-4fda-8937-a306cf6cc87c","uuid":"0f8e2b66-913d-4b4a-8e3b-a6d9bcc358aa","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:09:43.151Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-adceadaf824ea214","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
