{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad92478c56c6c046","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-E005\n3\ttitle: Document the default vector store, bring-your-own configuration, and migration\n4\t  path\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n6\tcomponent: Documentation\n7\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\timplementation_type: docs-authoring\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E002\n14\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E003\n15\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n16\tgate_failure_impact:\n17\t  action: rewrite\n18\t  fallback_approach: Documentation content is rewritten around the provisioning approach\n19\t    selected by the go/no-go decision; if no auto-provisioning ships, the documentation\n20\t    covers the bring-your-own PostgreSQL configuration posture instead.\n21\tai_signals:\n22\t  change_specificity: 1\n23\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n24\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n25\t  existing_foundation: 1\n26\t  open_questions: 0\n27\t  external_dependency: 0\n28\t  human_process_gates: -1\n29\t  repo_access: 1\n30\t  architecture_claims: 0\n31\tinvestigation_signals: null\n32\tai_implementability: High\n33\tai_implementability_score: 3\n34\tjira_key: null\n35\tbranch: null\n36\t---\n37\t# Document the Default Vector Store, Bring-Your-Own Configuration, and Migration Path\n38\t\n39\t## Description\n40\t\n41\tAuthor user-facing documentation for the default vector store capability: what Gen AI Studio\n42\tplayground users get out of the box, how the pgvector-backed vector store behaves, how to\n43\tconfigure a user-supplied (bring-your-own) PostgreSQL for RAG, and how to migrate from the\n44\tdefault vector store to a production-grade vector database. This resolves the strategy's open\n45\tquestion on the migration path (raised to align with commonly-used vector DB providers): the\n46\tdefault store is pgvector with a configurable connection, so migration is a documented\n47\tconfiguration change rather than new code. Documentation must be written after the\n48\timplementations deliver, and must reflect the provisioning approach selected by the go/no-go\n49\tdecision (operator-provisioned, BFF-provisioned, or bring-your-own posture).\n50\t\n51\t## Scope\n52\t\n53\t- New/updated doc topics covering:\n54\t  - The default vector store behavior for Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows (out-of-the-box\n55\t    experience, dev-experimentation scope and its limits).\n56\t  - The selected provisioning approach as delivered (auto-provisioned per the go/no-go decision,\n57\t    or bring-your-own configuration via the OGXServer CR spec and connection secret).\n58\t  - Bring-your-own PostgreSQL configuration for RAG capabilities (when users want their own\n59\t    database).\n60\t  - Migration path from the default vector store to an external/production-grade vector database,\n61\t    aligned with commonly-used vector DB providers.\n62\t  - Guidance that production-scale vector workloads should use an external vector database.\n63\t- Technically review all content against the delivered implementation and the architecture\n64\t  context before publication.\n65\t\n66\t## Acceptance Criteria\n67\t\n68\t- Documentation covers the default vector store behavior, the delivered provisioning approach,\n69\t  bring-your-own configuration, and the migration path to production-grade vector databases.\n70\t- All content is technically reviewed against the delivered implementation (provider\n71\t  configuration, wiring, and provisioning behavior) for accuracy.\n72\t- The migration-path topic addresses alignment with commonly-used vector DB providers via the\n73\t  configurable connection.\n74\t- No content implies manual setup steps are required for the out-of-the-box playground RAG\n75\t  experience in the auto-provisioned outcomes.\n76\t\n77\t## HLR Traceability\n78\t\n79\t- SE-2 (bring-your-own PostgreSQL configuration documented).\n80\t- SE-3 (migration path to a production-grade vector database documented).\n81\t- SE-6 (no additional manual setup steps — the documented out-of-the-box experience).\n82\t- AC-1/AC-2 (documented behavior of the delivered default vector store).\n83\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a5d9e3a32beb111a","agent_id":"a9d1510e518acea17","session_id":"546378e3-e46e-4fda-8937-a306cf6cc87c","uuid":"ea5435fb-b005-43ca-92b8-e154f97b9f27","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:09:47.435Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad92478c56c6c046","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
