{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8dfdf965fb16a602","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E006\n3\ttitle: Operator-based PostgreSQL/pgvector provisioning for Gen AI Studio (go outcome)\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n5\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n6\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: If RHAISTRAT-7164 does not deliver the RHOAI-controlled operator\n16\t    layer in time (no-go), this epic is removed and provisioning falls to the BFF-managed\n17\t    approach (branch B) or, if that proves unviable, the bring-your-own PostgreSQL\n18\t    posture with no auto-provisioning epic.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 1\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n23\t  existing_foundation: 0\n24\t  open_questions: 1\n25\t  external_dependency: -1\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 5\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Operator-Based PostgreSQL/pgvector Provisioning for Gen AI Studio (Go Outcome)\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tBranch outcome \"go\": the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) delivers the\n40\tRHOAI-controlled operator layer in time for the target release, and PostgreSQL/pgvector lifecycle\n41\tmanagement for Gen AI Studio playgrounds is implemented in that operator following the\n42\tmodel-registry-operator's auto-provisioning pattern. The operator provisions a PostgreSQL instance\n43\t(using the existing Red Hat `rhel9/postgresql-16` image, which includes pgvector out of the box —\n44\tno custom image build) scoped per the confirmed scoping model (per-namespace by default), and\n45\texposes the connection secret that the playground OGXServer wiring consumes. This branch exists\n46\tonly if the go/no-go decision selects the operator-based approach; the decision's external\n47\tprecondition is that RHAISTRAT-7164 actually delivers the operator layer.\n48\t\n49\t## Scope\n50\t\n51\t- Implement PostgreSQL/pgvector instance lifecycle management in the RHOAI-controlled operator\n52\t  layer delivered by the dashboard operator modularization, following the model-registry-operator\n53\t  pattern for auto-provisioned databases (Deployment, Service, credentials secret, and related\n54\t  resources).\n55\t- Use the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL image with pgvector; wire the image reference for\n56\t  disconnected installs following the existing related-image environment variable pattern already\n57\t  present in the platform operator CSV.\n58\t- Scope provisioned instances per the confirmed scoping model (per-namespace isolation by\n59\t  default).\n60\t- Expose the PostgreSQL connection secret in the playground namespace, satisfying the\n61\t  connection-secret contract consumed by the playground OGXServer vector_io wiring.\n62\t- Set resource requests/limits starting from the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL reference\n63\t  values, adjusted per benchmark findings.\n64\t- Handle lifecycle: provisioning on demand, and cleanup/garbage collection when the playground\n65\t  (or its namespace) is removed.\n66\t- Document the provisioning behavior for inclusion in the user-facing documentation.\n67\t\n68\t## Acceptance Criteria\n69\t\n70\t- A Gen AI Studio playground with RAG enabled gets a working PostgreSQL/pgvector instance\n71\t  provisioned automatically, with no manual user setup, in a cluster with the operator installed.\n72\t- The provisioned instance uses the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL image with pgvector (no custom\n73\t  image build, no new pipeline onboarding).\n74\t- The connection secret satisfies the contract consumed by the playground OGXServer vector_io\n75\t  wiring, and playground RAG works end-to-end against the provisioned instance.\n76\t- Instances are scoped per the confirmed scoping model (per-namespace isolation by default) —\n77\t  tenants in different namespaces do not share vector data.\n78\t- Resource requests/limits start from the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL reference values\n79\t  and are recorded with rationale (benchmark-adjusted where available).\n80\t- Provisioned resources are cleaned up when the playground is deleted.\n81\t- Disconnected-install support: the PostgreSQL image reference is resolvable via the\n82\t  related-image environment variable pattern.\n83\t\n84\t## HLR Traceability\n85\t\n86\t- AC-1 (default vector store available out-of-the-box, no manual provisioning).\n87\t- AC-2 (playground RAG workflows function with the default vector store) — provisioning completes\n88\t  the end-to-end path.\n89\t- AC-5 (multi-tenant scoping, per-namespace isolation).\n90\t- AC-6 (lightweight for resource-constrained environments) — resource sizing.\n91\t- SE-1 (model-registry-operator auto-provisioning pattern, no custom image).\n92\t- SE-6 (no additional manual setup steps).\n93\t- SE-8 (resource sizing from model-registry-operator reference).\n94\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a5d9e3a32beb111a","agent_id":"a9d1510e518acea17","session_id":"546378e3-e46e-4fda-8937-a306cf6cc87c","uuid":"a3de4bed-ad0e-484a-b9ab-4edbc0251c78","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:09:48.340Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8dfdf965fb16a602","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
