e\ncontradicts the rubric conditions or the strategy text.\n\n### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n\nEvery epic has concrete, testable ACs derived from the strategy and Staff input. Rule-mandated\nACs: E005 (docs-authoring) has the technical-review-against-implementation AC; no konflux-chain\nepics exist (N/A); no replacement epic requires a rollback/feature-flag AC — the inline Milvus\nremoval is RHAISTRAT-7474's scope, and the pgvector provider is env-guard activated\n(`ENABLE_PGVECTOR`), which is itself the activation switch. E004's ACs encode the Staff-defined\npass criterion (order of magnitude, no latency SLA). The branch epics include the\nend-to-end RAG validation, per-namespace isolation, resource-sizing rationale, cleanup, and\n(branch B) restart idempotency ACs — directly traceable to the Staff Engineer caveats. No epic\nbody references sibling epics by draft ID; cross-epic references use work descriptions or real\nticket keys (RHAISTRAT-7164, RHAISTRAT-7474).\n\n### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n\nAll strategy scope after Staff-Engineer filtering is accounted for: AC-1 (branch epics), AC-2\n(E002/E003/E004), AC-4 (E002/E003), AC-5 (E001 decision + branches), AC-6 (E004 sizing +\nbranches); both strategy open questions are resolved into explicit scope (scoping model into\nE001's decision record; migration path into E003's configurable connection plus E005\ndocumentation); Staff corrections are carried as documented overrides rather than dropped (no\nimage build/Konflux scope, vector_io-only configuration, SQLite untouched, Auto Rag decoupled,\nperformance thresholds removed, model-registry sizing reference). Conditional branches cover all\nthree bounded outcomes of the go/no-go: branch A (go), branch B (no-go, BFF-managed), and the\nbring-your-own outcome correctly modeled as a no-epic fallback recorded in branch B's\n`gate_failure_impact` and covered by E003 + E005. Cross-epic consistency holds: E002's provider,\nE003's wiring, and the branches' provisioning collectively account for every item in each\nother's scope via the connection-secret contract. A docs-authoring epic is present. Strategy-level\ncontext (risks, release-commitment risk, scope traps) is carried forward in Health Warnings\nrather than silently dropped.\n\nMinor: completeness could not be verified against the unavailable strategy attachment (NFRs,\ndependency table, affected-components table); the decomposition flags this itself and recommends\nhuman reconciliation before execution.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":39110,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a5d9e3a32beb111a","agent_id":"a9d1510e518acea17","session_id":"546378e3-e46e-4fda-8937-a306cf6cc87c","uuid":"464f2119-09de-4455-8bb4-30eb5e3e58e5","timestamp":"2026-10-21T19:13:11.845Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
