{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab76a4ac1c544e6c","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n3\tepic_count: 7\n4\tcritical_path_length: 2\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\trevised: true\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary: RHAISTRAT-8004 — Default Vector Store for Gen AI Studio\n11\t\n12\tRHAISTRAT-8004 delivers a default, out-of-the-box vector store (PostgreSQL with pgvector) so that\n13\tGen AI Studio playground RAG workflows continue to function when inline providers are removed from\n14\tthe OGX (Llama Stack) distribution per RHAISTRAT-7474. The strategy is Blocker priority and\n15\tstatus Release Pending.\n16\t\n17\t**Input fidelity note:** the full strategy text exceeds the Jira description size limit and is\n18\tstored as an attachment (`RHAISTRAT-8004-strategy.md`) that is not present in the pre-provisioned\n19\tworkspace. This decomposition is derived from the Jira issue body (Summary, Problem Statement,\n20\tAcceptance Criteria, Success Criteria, Open Questions) plus the detailed Staff Engineer Input,\n21\twhich takes precedence per Step 1.5. The Affected Components table, Impacted Teams table,\n22\tprioritized High Level Requirements, Dependencies table, and Non-Functional Requirements from the\n23\tattachment were unavailable; requirement traceability below maps the strategy's Acceptance\n24\tCriteria (post Staff-Engineer filtering) plus Staff-Engineer-derived requirements instead of HLR\n25\tIDs. See Health Warnings.\n26\t\n27\t## Epic List\n28\t\n29\t| ID | Title | Type | Component | Team | Priority |\n30\t|----|-------|------|-----------|------|----------|\n31\t| RHAISTRAT-8004-E001 | Default vector store provisioning approach go/no-go decision | Investigation | Gen AI Studio | Gen AI Studio | P0 |\n32\t| RHAISTRAT-8004-E002 | Enable and validate the remote pgvector vector_io provider in the OGX distribution | Implementation | OGX Core | OGX Core | P0 |\n33\t| RHAISTRAT-8004-E003 | Configure Gen AI Studio playground OGXServer instances to use a pgvector vector store | Implementation | Gen AI Studio | Gen AI Studio | P0 |\n34\t| RHAISTRAT-8004-E004 | Benchmark pgvector against the inline Milvus baseline for playground RAG and recommend resource sizing | Investigation | RAG + Vector DB | Gen AI Studio | P0 |\n35\t| RHAISTRAT-8004-E005 | Document the default vector store, bring-your-own configuration, and migration path | Implementation (docs-authoring) | Documentation | Gen AI Studio | P0 |\n36\t| RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E006 | Operator-based PostgreSQL/pgvector provisioning for Gen AI Studio (go outcome) | Implementation | Gen AI Studio | Gen AI Studio | P0 |\n37\t| RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-B-E006 | BFF-managed PostgreSQL/pgvector provisioning for Gen AI Studio playgrounds (no-go outcome) | Implementation | Gen AI Studio | Gen AI Studio | P0 |\n38\t\n39\tEpic count: 7 total (5 main-plan epics + 2 branch epics). Branch epics are conditional outcomes of\n40\tthe E001 go/no-go decision and are attached to the gating Investigation as a plan document; they\n41\tare not standalone main-plan nodes.\n42\t\n43\t## Dependency DAG\n44\t\n45\t```mermaid\n46\tgraph TD\n47\t    E001[\"E001 Provisioning approach go/no-go (Investigation)\"]\n48\t    E002[\"E002 OGX distribution pgvector provider\"]\n49\t    E003[\"E003 Playground pgvector wiring\"]\n50\t    E004[\"E004 pgvector benchmark and sizing\"]\n51\t    E005[\"E005 Documentation\"]\n52\t\n53\t    E001 --> BA[\"BRANCH-A-E006 Operator-based provisioning (branch A)\"]\n54\t    E001 --> BB[\"BRANCH-B-E006 BFF-managed provisioning (branch B)\"]\n55\t    E001 --> E005\n56\t    E002 --> E005\n57\t    E003 --> E005\n58\t\n59\t    E004 -.-> BA\n60\t    E004 -.-> BB\n61\t```\n62\t\n63\tSolid arrows are blocking DAG edges recorded in frontmatter `dependencies`. Dashed arrows are\n64\tinformational flows only (benchmark sizing results feed the provisioning epics as acceptance\n65\tcriteria / tuning input — no blocking edge; sizing starts from the model-registry-operator\n66\treference values per Staff Engineer Input). E001, E002, E003, and E004 are all roots and may start\n67\tin parallel (Tier 1).\n68\t\n69\t## DAG Justification\n70\t\n71\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n72\t|------|------|-----------|\n73\t| E001 → BRANCH-A-E006 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates downstream) | The go/no-go decision determines whether operator-based provisioning is built at all; true gate with `remove` semantics for the branch if the outcome is \"no-go\". |\n74\t| E001 → BRANCH-B-E006 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates downstream) | BFF-managed provisioning only exists if the no-go outcome selects it; true gate with `remove` semantics for the branch if the outcome is \"go\". |\n75\t| E001 → E005 | Rule 3 / Rule 11 | Documentation must describe the provisioning approach that was actually selected (operator-based, BFF-managed, or bring-your-own); the decision rewrites the doc content. |\n76\t| E002 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring blocked by all Implementations) | Docs describe the delivered pgvector provider capability. |\n77\t| E003 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring blocked by all Implementations) | Docs describe the delivered playground wiring and user-facing behavior. |\n78\t| E004 ⇢ (dashed, no edge) provisioning epics | Rule 4 / AC gate | Benchmark results are informational for sizing (start from model-registry-operator reference; adjust per benchmark). Failure means tune-and-retry, not different epics. |\n79\t| No edge E002 → E003 | Rule 13 carve-out | The distribution's pgvector provider is consumed by the playground via configuration (activation env var / CR spec), not a build-against artifact; the contract already exists (`ENABLE_PGVECTOR`, remote::pgvector). Wired as an acceptance criterion on E003 (\"validated against an OGX distribution build that includes the remote pgvector provider\"), not a DAG edge. |\n80\t| No edge E001 → E002/E003/E004 | Step 5.5 Tier 1 | pgvector enablement, playground wiring, and benchmarking deliver independent value with any PostgreSQL endpoint (including bring-your-own); they are not gated by the provisioning decision. |\n81\t| No edge konflux-onboarding / repo-onboarding / license-validation | Rules 5–10 (not applicable) | Staff Engineer Correction 2: the Red Hat `rhel9/postgresql-16` image already includes pgvector and is already referenced by the rhods-operator CSV (`RELATED_IMAGE_POSTGRESQL_16_IMAGE`) for disconnected installs. No new image build, no new repo, no Konflux onboarding chain. |\n82\t| No edge from branch epics to E005 | Conditional-decomposition rule 2 | Main-plan epics must not depend on branch epics; docs cover the selected approach generically and the branch epics carry provisioning-specific documentation as scope/AC. E005's publication step explicitly incorporates the selected branch's provisioning documentation (lifecycle behavior, limits, resource-sizing rationale) so the branch-contributed content reaches the user-facing docs without a DAG edge. |\n83\t\n84\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n85\t\n86\tThe HLR table from the strategy attachment was unavailable. Requirements are derived from the\n87\tstrategy's Acceptance Criteria (numbered AC-n, after Staff-Engineer filtering) and\n88\tStaff-Engineer-derived requirements (numbered SE-n):\n89\t\n90\t| Requirement | Text (abridged) | Epics |\n91\t|-------------|-----------------|-------|\n92\t| AC-1 | Default vector store available out-of-the-box, no manual provisioning/configuration | BRANCH-A-E006, BRANCH-B-E006 |\n93\t| AC-2 | Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function with the default vector store, no loss of capability | E002, E003, E004 |\n94\t| AC-3 (removed) | Auto Rag functions with the default vector store | Removed from scope per Staff Engineer Input (Auto Rag compatibility is RHAISTRAT-7824 scope, targeting RHOAI 3.6) — see Overrides |\n95\t| AC-4 | Vector store runs as a separate process, decoupled from the OGX instance (not inline) | E002, E003 |\n96\t| AC-5 | Scoped appropriately for multi-tenant environments (per-namespace isolation) | E001 (decision), BRANCH-A-E006, BRANCH-B-E006 |\n97\t| AC-6 | Lightweight enough for resource-constrained environments | E004 (sizing), BRANCH-A-E006, BRANCH-B-E006 |\n98\t| SE-1 | Self-provisioning pattern follows the model-registry-operator auto-provisioned PostgreSQL pattern; no custom image build | BRANCH-A-E006 |\n99\t| SE-2 | Bring-your-own PostgreSQL supported via user-configured connection secret in the OGXServer CR spec | E003, E005 |\n100\t| SE-3 | Migration path from the default vector store to a production-grade vector database (align with commonly-used providers) | E003 (configurable connection), E005 (documentation) |\n101\t| SE-4 | Portability: consume a platform-provided shared connection string when the DSC-managed shared PostgreSQL arrives (RHOAI 3.6) | E003, BRANCH-B-E006 |\n102\t| SE-5 | Vector storage (vector_io) configuration only; OGX application storage remains SQLite — no storage migration | E003 (constraint) |\n103\t| SE-6 | No additional manual setup steps for RAG workflows vs the current experience | BRANCH-A-E006, BRANCH-B-E006, E003 |\n104\t| SE-7 | Benchmark captures inline Milvus baseline; pgvector within same order of magnitude (dev-experimentation scope, no strict SLAs; flat scan acceptable) | E004 |\n105\t| SE-8 | Resource sizing starts from model-registry-operator PostgreSQL requests/limits, adjusted per benchmark | BRANCH-A-E006, BRANCH-B-E006, E004 |\n106\t\n107\tAll post-filtering requirements are covered; no orphans.\n108\t\n109\t## Conditional Branches\n110\t\n111\tThe go/no-go decision (E001) has bounded outcomes (≤3) that change which provisioning\n112\tImplementation exists:\n113\t\n114\t- **Branch A — \"go\"**: RHAISTRAT-7164 (dashboard operator modularization) delivers the\n115\t  RHOAI-controlled operator layer in time. PostgreSQL/pgvector lifecycle management is implemented\n116\t  in that operator following the model-registry-operator pattern. External precondition: the\n117\t  RHAISTRAT-7164 operator layer must actually land; it is tracked by E001 and is not an epic in\n118\t  this strategy. → `RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E006.md`\n119\t- **Branch B — \"no-go, BFF-managed\"**: RHAISTRAT-7164 does not land in time, and the gen-ai BFF\n120\t  provisions the PostgreSQL/pgvector instance directly (Deployment, Service, PVC, Secret) when a\n121\t  playground with RAG is configured — the same pattern the BFF already uses for guardrails\n122\t  infrastructure. → `RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-B-E006.md`\n123\t- **Branch C — \"no-go, bring-your-own\" (no branch epic)**: if BFF-managed provisioning is judged\n124\t  unviable (lifecycle management caveats), the ultimate fallback is customers bringing their own\n125\t  PostgreSQL, manually configuring the OGXServer CR spec with their connection details. This\n126\t  outcome requires no auto-provisioning epic: it is covered by E003's configurable\n127\t  connection-secret wiring (SE-2) plus E005 documentation. Recorded as the\n128\t  `gate_failure_impact` fallback on branch B.\n129\t\n130\t## Staff Engineer Input Overrides\n131\t\n132\tThe Staff Engineer Input takes precedence over the AI-generated strategy (which resides in the\n133\tunavailable attachment). Overrides applied:\n134\t\n135\t1. **OGX does not auto-provision PostgreSQL** — OGX application storage defaults to SQLite\n136\t   (`storage.kv.type: sqlite`, `storage.sql.type: sqlite`); the gen-ai BFF hardcodes SQLite when\n137\t   creating OGXServer instances. The strategy's \"every LlamaStackDistribution instance requires\n138\t   PostgreSQL\" claim is wrong; introducing PostgreSQL for vector storage is new work.\n139\t2. **No custom image build or Konflux onboarding** — `registry.redhat.io/rhel9/postgresql-16`\n140\t   already includes pgvector; model-registry-operator already auto-provisions it and\n141\t   `RELATED_IMAGE_POSTGRESQL_16_IMAGE` is already in the rhods-operator CSV. The strategy's 1–2\n142\t   sprint image-onboarding estimate is eliminated; no onboarding-chain epics were generated.\n143\t3. **Vector storage is independent of application storage** — only the vector_io provider\n144\t   (`remote::pgvector` via `ENABLE_PGVECTOR`) is configured; application storage stays SQLite. All\n145\t   SQLite-to-PostgreSQL migration / storage-consolidation scope from the strategy is removed.\n146\t4. **Hard dependency on RHAISTRAT-7164** for operator-based self-provisioning; ogx-k8s-operator is\n147\t   upstream and cannot carry RHOAI-specific provisioning logic. Modeled as the E001 go/no-go gate\n148\t   with conditional branches rather than a linear blocking edge.\n149\t5. **Fallbacks defined**: bring-your-own PostgreSQL (users configure the OGXServer CR spec) and the\n150\t   BFF-managed provisioning alternative; a go/no-go gate is to be defined during sprint planning —\n151\t   modeled as Investigation E001.\n152\t6. **Auto Rag decoupled** — removed from affected components, teams, acceptance criteria, and\n153\t   validation; Auto Rag pgvector compatibility is RHAISTRAT-7824 scope (RHOAI 3.6). AC-3 dropped.\n154\t7. **Performance thresholds removed** — dev-experimentation scope; order-of-magnitude benchmark\n155\t   against the inline Milvus baseline only; flat scan (no index) is sufficient for typical\n156\t   playground document sets; users with production-scale workloads should use an external vector\n157\t   database. No latency-SLA, corpus-size, or index-selection epics or investigations were created.\n158\t8. **Resource sizing** starts from the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL requests/limits,\n159\t   adjusted per sprint-1 benchmarking — an AC on the provisioning epics, not a blocking edge.\n160\t9. **Remote vector store implementation is reusable** — the existing remote vector store\n161\t   implementation covers most of the provider integration; the majority of effort is\n162\t   infrastructure/provisioning. Provider work is a single focused epic (E002), not a large\n163\t   integration program.\n164\t\n165\t## Health Warnings\n166\t\n167\t- **Missing strategy attachment (input fidelity)**: the Affected Components, Impacted Teams, HLR,\n168\t  Dependencies, and NFR tables live in `RHAISTRAT-8004-strategy.md`, which was not available.\n169\t  Team assignments below are inferred (Gen AI Studio for dashboard/BFF/docs work, OGX Core for the\n170\t  distribution); the traceability matrix uses acceptance criteria instead of HLR IDs. A human\n171\t  should reconcile this decomposition against the attachment before execution.\n172\t- **Release-commitment risk (priority inversion risk)**: the strategy is Blocker / Release\n173\t  Pending, yet its primary provisioning path is gated on RHAISTRAT-7164 (In Progress) with\n174\t  uncertain timing. The Staff Engineer explicitly notes it will be \"challenging to commit this\n175\t  strategy to a specific release until that dependency is delivered.\" The go/no-go gate (E001) is\n176\t  correctly P0 and first — do not let the release-pending status force starting a provisioning\n177\t  branch before the gate resolves.\n178\t- **Scope trap avoided**: the AI-generated strategy's image build + Konflux onboarding chain\n179\t  (1–2 sprints) was eliminated by Staff Engineer Correction 2 — the pgvector-capable image already\n180\t  exists. Any re-introduction of image-building scope should be challenged.\n181\t- **Multi-tenant scoping**: the strategy's open question on per-namespace vs per-instance scoping\n182\t  is largely resolved by Staff direction (per-namespace preferred; the per-instance driver —\n183\t  Auto Rag — is decoupled), but it is confirmed as part of the E001 decision record rather than\n184\t  assumed.\n185\t- **Open question retained as documentation scope**: the migration-path question (alignment with\n186\t  commonly-used vector DB providers) is resolved as a configurable-connection AC plus\n187\t  documentation (E005), not as a gating investigation — the pgvector default already aligns with\n188\t  commonly-used providers and migration is configuration, not new code.\n189\t\n190\t## Tiered Delivery\n191\t\n192\tExternal dependency with uncertain timing: RHAISTRAT-7164 (dashboard operator modularization).\n193\tPartial value is deliverable without it, so the strategy splits:\n194\t\n195\t- **Tier 1 (independent, start immediately)**: E001 (go/no-go decision — sprint-planning gate),\n196\t  E002 (OGX distribution pgvector provider), E003 (playground wiring, works against any\n197\t  PostgreSQL endpoint including bring-your-own), E004 (benchmark and sizing — risk-reduction\n198\t  validation).\n199\t- **Tier 2 (dependency-gated)**: the provisioning branch epics (BRANCH-A-E006 / BRANCH-B-E006),\n200\t  gated by the E001 decision; BRANCH-A-E006 is additionally preconditioned on RHAISTRAT-7164\n201\t  actually delivering the operator layer.\n202\t- **E005 (documentation)** runs last, blocked by the Tier 1 Implementations and the E001 decision.\n203\t\n204\t## Component Mappings\n205\t\n206\tCanonical RHAI component names used (from `.context/rhai-components.txt`); non-obvious mappings:\n207\t\n208\t- OGX distribution (repo `ogx-distribution`, formerly llama-stack distribution) → **OGX Core**\n209\t- Gen AI Studio playground / gen-ai BFF / OGXServer wiring (repo `odh-dashboard`) → **Gen AI Studio**\n210\t- pgvector benchmark for RAG workloads → **RAG + Vector DB** (executed by the Gen AI Studio team)\n211\t- User-facing documentation → **Documentation**\n212\t\n213\tAll touched components exist in `.context/architecture-context/` (odh-dashboard, ogx-distribution,\n214\togx-k8s-operator, model-registry-operator, rhods-operator) — no new-component onboarding chains\n215\twere generated (see Override 2).\n216\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9877e6791d4a2494","agent_id":"a0e76211b5f33ff08","session_id":"546378e3-e46e-4fda-8937-a306cf6cc87c","uuid":"c10eff54-962c-4f